{
 "$comment": [
   "G12 corpus of the single quality gate (RC-122; REQ-SAFE-052): realistic series descriptions and the class the gate must give. DRAFT, PENDING owner approval.",
   "Read by backend/tests/unit/test_quality_gate_matrix.py (sequence_from_header) AND frontend/src/services/qualityGate/gate.test.ts (sequenceFromHeader): both rules must give these classes (G4).",
   "Classes: FLAIR (only an unambiguous FLAIR, T2-FLAIR or dark-fluid name), T1, T2, other (any token naming a non-FLAIR sequence, a T1 weighting with FLAIR, a localizer, a derived/reformatted/contrast image, or an inversion time < 1400 ms: ALWAYS abstains, whatever the physician confirms), unknown (names no sequence: confirmable in a single study), missing (nothing recorded).",
   "Second review of PR #81 (G15, restated in the fifth): with the gate ON, ONE classifier — the gate (backend and browser) and the RC-049 header evidence of the in-browser AI give these classes (with the gate off RC-049 keeps its base rules, and the research inventory always does, G26); TIRM is a FLAIR (as RC-049 already read it), 'TI=' / 'TI:' in the text is an inversion time (seconds below 10).",
   "Third review of PR #81 (G19): classification is FIELD-AWARE. 'text' is the description (SeriesDescription, ProtocolName, NIfTI descrip); 'sequence_name' is the DICOM SequenceName, a vendor internal code read by its own table ('*' is a Siemens prefix there, never 'T2*'; an unlisted code says nothing); 'image_type' is the DICOM ImageType (a reformatted, projected, subtracted or parametric image is 'other', D-QG-7; anything else says nothing).",
   "Seventh review of PR #81 (S1): DICOM ImageType entries - a derived, secondary, resampled, reformatted, projected, subtracted, localizer or screen-save image is other; an original (and its vendor flags) says nothing. Fifth review of PR #81 (D-QG-12): the weak words cal, loc, dir and mag make an image other only when the description names no FLAIR; pha, pc, epi, trace and every other word of the other list always do."
 ],
